<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Online Exam</title>
<style>
body {
font-family: Arial,sans-serif; 
background: #f4f4f4; 
padding: 20px;
}
.exam-box { 
background: #fff; 
padding: 20px; 
max-width: 600px; 
margin: auto; 
border-radius: 5px;
}
button {
margin-top: 15px; 
padding: 10px 20px; 
font-size: 15px; 
cursor: pointer;
}
.result {
font-size: 18px; 
margin-top: 20px; 
font-weight: bold;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="exam-box">
<h2>Online Exam</h2>
<form id="examForm">
<p>1. JavaScript is a language.</p>
<input type="radio" name="q1" value="a"> Markup<br>
<input type="radio" name="q1" value="b"> Programming<br>
<input type="radio" name="q1" value="c"> Styling<br><br>
<p>2. Which tag is used to write JavaScript?</p>
<input type="radio" name="q2" value="a"> &lt;js&gt;<br>
<input type="radio" name="q2" value="b"> &lt;javascript&gt;<br>
<input type="radio" name="q2" value="c"> &lt;script&gt;<br><br>
<p>3. Which keyword is used to declare a variable?</p>
<input type="radio" name="q3" value="a"> int<br>
<input type="radio" name="q3" value="b"> var<br>
<input type="radio" name="q3" value="c"> string<br><br>
<button type="button" onclick="submitExam()">Submit Exam</button>
</form>
<div class="result" id="result"></div>
</div>
<script>
function submitExam() { 
let score = 0;
if (document.querySelector('input[name="q1"]:checked')?.value === "b") score++; 
if (document.querySelector('input[name="q2"]:checked')?.value === "c") score++; 
if (document.querySelector('input[name="q3"]:checked')?.value === "b") score++;
document.getElementById("result").innerHTML = 
"Your Score: " + score + " / 3";
}
</script>
</body>
</html>
